WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.788
Three more client decisions.

2
00:00:01.788 --> 00:00:05.750
First, D N S over H T T P S.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.651
The client doesn't support secure D N S,

4
00:00:08.651 --> 00:00:14.171
so an Intune settings catalog profile
sets Control the mode of D N S over

5
00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:19.037
H T T P S to Disabled, in Edge and
Chrome, assigned to the same group.

6
00:00:19.037 --> 00:00:20.613
Second, hardening.

7
00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:23.818
Learn's remediation scripts
can hide the disable and

8
00:00:23.818 --> 00:00:26.951
sign-out buttons and restrict
non-privileged users.

9
00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:32.286
Learn's advice is to let users run
unrestricted first and confirm nobody needs

10
00:00:32.286 --> 00:00:37.212
to disable the client, for a website or
a parallel V P N, before restricting.

11
00:00:37.212 --> 00:00:41.462
So the guide deploys the remediation
from ring two, not in the pilot.

12
00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:45.746
Third, upgrades, in rings: a
new app for each new version,

13
00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:50.712
assigned to a small group, widened,
and the old app deleted last.

14
00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:53.187
Rolling back re-assigns the previous app.

15
00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:59.620
And don't disable QUIC in browsers for
this; Step 5 handles QUIC, in Module 5.
